  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - Due to inaccurate drawings the council are unable to ascertain the impact on the character and appearance of the host site or the surrounding area nor are they able to assess the impact on neighbour amenity. It is therefore concluded that the proposal would fail to comply with the principles of policies D3 and D4 of the London Plan 2021 and policies D12.1, D12.3 and D12.4 of Merton Local Plan 2024",
    "Reason : 2 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice \r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance:\r\n\"\tThe application was not considered to comply with the provisions of the Development Plan and NPPF as submitted, and would have required substantial changes such that a new application would be required. \r\n\"\tIt is noted that the applicant/agent did not engage in any pre-application discussions.\r\n\"\tThe applicant is advised to seek pre-application advice on any resubmission.\r\n",
    "Reason : 3 - INFORMATIVE: The applicant/agent is reminded to review the validation requirements which include a Site Location Plan and Block Plan. All drawings must be to scale, regardless of annotations.",
    "Reason : 4 - INFORMATIVE: Every drawing must have their own drawing number"
  ],
